# Neutral Test Fixture Names

Do not use real operator, teammate, friend, or customer names/handles/emails in
test fixtures, snapshots, mock users, comments, or expected strings.

Use role-based or synthetic names instead:

- Good: `Sender`, `Recipient`, `Agent Owner`, `Room Admin`, `Guest User`
- Good: `Test User A`, `Test User B`, `Bot Alpha`, `Bot Beta`
- Good handles/emails: `sender`, `recipient`, `agent-owner`, `user-a@test.local`
- Avoid: real people names, real handles, or personal email-shaped fixtures.

If a test needs multiple humans, name them by role in the scenario:
`requester`, `recipient`, `roomOwner`, `agentOwner`, `viewer`.
